  "content_html": "<p>I am old enough to remember when I posted this yesterday on X and got a huge amount of shit for it, from Sabine Hossenfelder and a slew of bots and tech bros:</p><div class=\"twitter-embed\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://x.com/garymarcus/status/2117988151734005874?a=AiQtKd8nehFgemh5mlI&amp;s=61&quot;,&quot;full_text&quot;:&quot;tech stocks set to crash now that people know that AI companies will no longer get a free ride.&quot;,&quot;username&quot;:&quot;GaryMarcus&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Gary Marcus&quot;,&quot;profile_image_url&quot;:&quot;https://pbs.substack.com/profile_images/2048405471900606464/kPeRHI2z_normal.jpg&quot;,&quot;date&quot;:&quot;2026-11-04T14:31:40.000Z&quot;,&quot;photos&quot;:[],&quot;quoted_tweet&quot;:{},&quot;reply_count&quot;:62,&quot;retweet_count&quot;:96,&quot;like_count&quot;:891,&quot;impression_count&quot;:45425,&quot;expanded_url&quot;:null,&quot;video_url&quot;:null,&quot;video_preview_media_key&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false}\" data-component-name=\"Twitter2ToDOM\"></div><p>And, yesterday, after I posted it, the market was actually mixed, split hard between chipmakers and neocloud companies like CoreWeave that got hit hard (much as I anticipated), and big companies like Amazon, Apple, and Google that didn&#8217;t, and instead got a bounce. </p><p>One theory was that people were rotating out of the smaller neocloud companies, and into the bigger tech companies that could better weather the cash crunch:</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!v286!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd9a4f051-c65b-4ef6-b067-52e706e5e4f5_1528x1432.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!v286!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd9a4f051-c65b-4ef6-b067-52e706e5e4f5_1528x1432.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!v286!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd9a4f051-c65b-4ef6-b067-52e706e5e4f5_1528x1432.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!v286!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd9a4f051-c65b-4ef6-b067-52e706e5e4f5_1528x1432.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!v286!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd9a4f051-c65b-4ef6-b067-52e706e5e4f5_1528x1432.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!v286!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd9a4f051-c65b-4ef6-b067-52e706e5e4f5_1528x1432.png\" width=\"1456\" height=\"1365\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/d9a4f051-c65b-4ef6-b067-52e706e5e4f5_1528x1432.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:1365,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:429479,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:true,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://garymarcus.substack.com/i/223645207?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd9a4f051-c65b-4ef6-b067-52e706e5e4f5_1528x1432.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!v286!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd9a4f051-c65b-4ef6-b067-52e706e5e4f5_1528x1432.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!v286!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd9a4f051-c65b-4ef6-b067-52e706e5e4f5_1528x1432.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!v286!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd9a4f051-c65b-4ef6-b067-52e706e5e4f5_1528x1432.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!v286!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd9a4f051-c65b-4ef6-b067-52e706e5e4f5_1528x1432.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" fetchpriority=\"high\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>Another similar theory was the hyperscalers were up because (in light of the public resistance to data centers which came clear on Tuesday) investors thought that the hyperscalers might finally settle down on their wild CapEx expenditures: </p><div class=\"twitter-embed\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://x.com/_nathancalvin/status/2118070894186713558?a=3-5BhI4_i_qPJgHzjIg&amp;s=61&quot;,&quot;full_text&quot;:&quot;Fascinating - Josh at Epoch thinks that hyperscaler stocks are up because investors want company management to spend less capex dollars building AI data centers and the election results will force them to comply&quot;,&quot;username&quot;:&quot;_NathanCalvin&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Nathan Calvin&quot;,&quot;profile_image_url&quot;:&quot;https://pbs.substack.com/profile_images/1976484090426634240/YFgYic9h_normal.jpg&quot;,&quot;date&quot;:&quot;2026-11-04T20:00:27.000Z&quot;,&quot;photos&quot;:[],&quot;quoted_tweet&quot;:{&quot;full_text&quot;:&quot;@billyhumblebrag investors disagree with management on capex and want them to build fewer data centers&quot;,&quot;username&quot;:&quot;justjoshinyou13&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Josh You&quot;,&quot;profile_image_url&quot;:&quot;https://pbs.substack.com/profile_images/1604174784643928064/01y26Fjz_normal.jpg&quot;,&quot;photos&quot;:[]},&quot;reply_count&quot;:4,&quot;retweet_count&quot;:1,&quot;like_count&quot;:65,&quot;impression_count&quot;:2758,&quot;expanded_url&quot;:null,&quot;video_url&quot;:null,&quot;video_preview_media_key&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false}\" data-component-name=\"Twitter2ToDOM\"></div><p>Today looks pretty different. It&#8217;s a slaughter. Almost no company is exempt.</p>\n      <p>\n          <a href=\"https://garymarcus.substack.com/p/breaking-mayhem-in-the-market\">\n              Read more\n          </a>\n      </p>",
